# Line endings are part of this repository's evidence, not a cosmetic detail.
#
# gap_metrics.py and hybrid_spec.py are frozen specifications whose SHA-256 is
# recorded in results_v3/confirmatory/*.json and is intended for public
# registration. spec_hash() hashes the file on disk, so a checkout that
# rewrites line endings changes the hash and makes a correct registration look
# falsified.
#
# This repository was authored with core.autocrlf=true, which stores LF and
# checks out CRLF on Windows. Without the rule below, the same commit yields
# be694e9b... on Linux and 5b80aec1... on Windows for the identical file.
#
# LF is pinned everywhere so every checkout reproduces the registered hash.
# hybrid_spec.spec_hash() additionally normalizes CRLF before hashing, so the
# registered value survives even a checkout that ignores this file.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary and vendored files that must not be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.bst -text
*.cls -text
*.sty -text
